<div class="content-wrap">

  <div class="content-card">
    <h2>Celsius to Fahrenheit Formula</h2>
    <p>To convert <strong>Celsius to Fahrenheit</strong>, multiply the temperature by 9/5 (or 1.8) then add 32. To go the other way, subtract 32 then divide by 1.8.</p>
    <div class="formula-box">°F = (°C × 1.8) + 32 &nbsp;|&nbsp; °C = (°F − 32) ÷ 1.8</div>
    <div class="tip-box">
      <span class="tip-icon">🌡️</span>
      <p><strong>Quick estimate:</strong> Double the Celsius value and add 30. Example: 20°C → 20×2+30 = 70°F (actual: 68°F). Works best between -10°C and 40°C.</p>
    </div>
    <h3>Key reference temperatures</h3>
